# Nothing of this pipeline's own. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for tools/rewrite-lore.mjs,
# DATABASE_URL and CURSEFORGE_TOKEN are all shared with the other pipelines or the site, so
# they live in the repo root's .env instead:
#
#     cp .env.example .env        # from the repo root
#
# tools/lib/env.mjs reads that file and then this directory's .env over it, so a
# pipelines/places/.env is still the place for anything that is this pipeline's alone.
# There is nothing in that category today, which is why this file sets nothing.
#
# NO ELEVENLABS KEY IS NEEDED HERE. Nothing in this pipeline talks to ElevenLabs: every
# request is the site's, from the droplet, with a key belonging to the signed-in editor.
# The tools here report on lines, build the addon's data files and check them. The root
# .env does carry ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, for the quests and books pipelines, which generate
# their own.
#
# The site's accounts (BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, BETTER_AUTH_URL) and the master key its stored
# ElevenLabs credentials are sealed with (SPOKEN_SECRET_KEY) are in apps/web/.env.local,
# because `next dev` runs inside apps/web. Locally all three have working defaults; in
# production all three are required and live in the droplet's shared/app.env -- see
# deploy/web/README.md.
#
# Registering grants no permissions, by design. Promote your local account by hand:
#   psql -d spoken_quests_dev \
#     -c "update \"user\" set role = 'editor' where email = 'you@example.com'"
#
# Nothing below is set locally, and setting any of it here would be a mistake.
#
# Every path under tools/ derives from ROOT in tools/lib/loredata.mjs, which is the
# module's own location -- correct for a script, and impossible once webpack has
# compiled it, because webpack replaces import.meta.url at build time. So the deployed
# site is told where its files are instead. These are the four, listed here so they are
# discoverable from the same place as everything else. They were ZONELORE_* until the two
# sites merged; the deployment they configure is /srv/spoken, and a variable naming
# the tree it no longer lives in is a variable somebody sets on the wrong box:
#
#   SPOKEN_PLACES_ROOT           the repo root: lore corpus, tools/voice/config*.json and pronunciation.json
#   SPOKEN_PLACES_SOUNDS         the audio store
#   SPOKEN_PLACES_AUDIO_HISTORY  superseded takes
#   SPOKEN_PLACES_MANIFEST       tools/voice/manifest.json
#
# Unset, each falls back to exactly the path it always had. The deployment's
# ecosystem.config.js is the only place they are set, and its README explains the split
# between the ones that live in a release and the ones that must not.
